hadiths[64]{hadithnumber,text}:
"908","Narrated from Sayyiduna Mu’ammar bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he sent his slave with one sa’ of wheat and said, “Sell this and bring back what you get.” The slave went and brought back one sa’ and a little more of barley. When he came to Mu’ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him, Mu’ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Why did you do this? Go and return it, and do not take except equal for equal. Because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘Sell grain for grain, equal for equal.’ And in those days our grain was barley. People said, ‘There is a difference between barley and wheat (so excess should be permissible).’ But he said, ‘I fear that both may be considered of the same type.’”"
"909","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever buys grain should not sell it until he has taken possession of it. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I consider this to apply to everything."
"910","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said to Marwan bin Al-Hakam (the governor of Madinah): ""Have you made the sale of usury lawful?"" Marwan said: ""Why, what have I done?"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""You have permitted the sale of receipts, whereas the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of grain until it is taken into possession."" Then Marwan addressed the people and forbade them from selling receipts. (The narrator of the hadith) Sulaiman says: ""I saw the guards snatching those receipts from the people."
"911","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever buys grain should not sell it until he has taken possession of it. And we used to buy grain in heaps from the riders, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade us from selling that heap before moving it from its place."
"912","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of Muzabana, and that is when one sells the fruit of his garden—if it is dates—for measured dry dates, or if it is grapes—for measured dry raisins, or if it is a field—for measured dry grain. He (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade all of these (because there is a possibility of excess or deficiency in all of them)."
"913","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah and Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a man from Banu Adi as the administrator of Khaybar. He brought Janib (a superior type of) dates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him, ""Are all the dates of Khaybar like this?"" He replied, ""No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah! We buy one sa' of this date for two sa' of mixed dates."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Do not do so. Rather, take them equal for equal, or sell one kind and buy the other with its price. And similarly, if you sell by weight, then sell equal for equal."
"914","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling a heap of dates whose weight is unknown in exchange for measured or known-weight dates."
"915","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling fruits before they ripen (that is, until they are safe from calamity, etc.), or he said: We were forbidden to sell fruits until they are safe (from calamity, etc.)."
"916","Abu Al-Bakhtari (may Allah have mercy on him) says: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about the sale of date palm trees (that is, selling their fruits), so he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of dates until they become fit to be eaten, fed, or stored after being cut. (The narrator says) I asked, ""What is meant by 'yuzan'?"" So a person sitting with him said, ""It means when they become fit to be cut and stored."
"917","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling dates until they become red or yellow (because when redness or yellowness appears in them, safety is assured), and likewise, he forbade selling ears (of grain) until they become white and are safe from calamity. He forbade the seller from selling and the buyer from buying."
"918","Bashir bin Yasar, the freed slave of Banu Haritha, narrates that Sayyiduna Rafi’ bin Khadij and Sahl bin Abi Hathmah (may Allah be pleased with them) told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of Muzabana (i.e., selling dates on the tree in exchange for dried dates), except for the owners of ‘Araya, to whom he permitted it. (This refers to those poor people to whom an orchard owner gives a tree, saying that they may use its fruit.)"
"919","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted in the case of ‘Ariyyah (the definition of which has been mentioned in the previous hadith) that the people of a household may give an estimated amount of dried dates and in exchange purchase fresh dates on the tree to eat."
"920","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, permitted the sale of ‘Araya by estimation, provided it is less than five wasq or up to five wasq (the narrator of the hadith, Dawood, is in doubt whether he said five wasq or less than five wasq)."
"921","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If you sell fruit to your brother and then some calamity befalls it (causing the fruit to perish), then it is not lawful for you to take anything from him. For what will you take your brother’s wealth—will you take it unjustly?"
"922","'Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that' a man bought fruit from a tree during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), which was destroyed by a natural calamity and he became heavily indebted (due to the loss of the fruit). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said that he should be given charity. People gave him charity, but even that did not cover his debt. Finally, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to his creditors, ""Now take whatever you have received, and you will not get anything more."
"923","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever buys a date-palm tree after it has been pollinated, its fruit belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates (otherwise). And whoever buys a slave, his property belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates (otherwise). (Bai‘ is the seller and Mushtari is the buyer.)"
"924","Zaid bin Abi Anisah says: Abu Al-Waleed Makki narrated to us from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he was sitting with Ata bin Abi Rabah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of Muhaqalah and Mukhabarah, and also forbade buying date-palm trees until their fruit becomes red or yellow or fit for eating. And Muhaqalah is when a standing crop is sold in exchange for a specified amount of grain. And Muzabanah is when the fruit of a date-palm tree is sold in exchange for a certain weight of dried dates. And Mukhabarah is when land is given for cultivation in exchange for a third or a quarter of the produce, or something similar (which in our country is called Bataai). Zaid said: I asked Ata bin Abi Rabah, ""Did you hear this hadith from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), that he narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He said, ""Yes."
"925","Abu Zubair and Saeed bin Mina narrate that Syedna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade Muhaqala, Muzabana, Muawama, and Mukhabara. (One of the narrators said that Muawama means selling the fruit of one's tree for several years.) And he forbade Istisna (i.e., taking out an unknown quantity, such as saying, ""I sold you this grain but will take a little out of it,"" or ""I sold this orchard but did not sell some of its trees,"" because in this case the sale becomes invalid. But if the exception is known, such as saying, ""I sold this heap of grain but will take out a quarter of it,"" then by consensus it is valid.) And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted 'Araya."
"926","`Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling (i.e., trees or land) for several years, and in the narration of Ibn Abi Shaybah, it is mentioned that he forbade the sale of fruit for several years."
"927","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a slave came and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for migration. But the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not know that he was a slave. Then his owner came to take him back, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Sell him to me."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) bought him by giving two black slaves. After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would not take allegiance from anyone until he asked whether he was a slave or free."
"928","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a goat whose udder is full of milk has the option for three days; if he wishes, he may keep it, or if he wishes, he may return it, and along with it, he should give one sa’ of dates."
"929","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) received news that Sayyiduna Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) had sold wine, so he said: May Allah curse Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him)! Does he not know the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that Allah Almighty cursed the Jews (because) fat was made unlawful for them, so they melted it and sold it."
"930","‘Abdur Rahman bin Wa’lah as-Sabbi (who was a resident of Egypt) narrates that he asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about the juice of grapes. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that a man brought a waterskin of wine as a gift for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Do you know that Allah Almighty has made it unlawful?” The man replied, “No.” Then he whispered something to another person. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “What did you say?” He replied, “I told him to sell it.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “The One (Allah) who has forbidden its drinking has also forbidden its selling.” (Upon hearing this) the man opened the mouth of the waterskin and poured out whatever was in it."
"931","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that in the year Makkah was conquered, he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in Makkah saying that Allah Almighty and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of alcohol, carrion, swine, and idols. The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the ruling regarding the fat of carrion? For it is used to caulk ships, it is applied to hides, and people use it for lighting."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""No, it is forbidden."" Then at that very moment he said, ""May Allah destroy the Jews! When Allah made fat forbidden for them (i.e., its consumption), they melted it, then sold it and consumed its price."
"932","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the gift of a soothsayer."
"933","Abu Zubair says: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) about the price of a dog and the price of a cat, so he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) strictly forbade it."
"934","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Rafi' bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The price of a dog is impure, the earnings of a prostitute are impure, and the earnings of a cupper are impure."
"935","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` a slave of Banu Bayadah cupped the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his wages. And he interceded with his master to reduce his tax. If (the wages of the cupper) were unlawful, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would never have given him wages."
"936","Humayd reports: Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the earnings of a cupping practitioner. He said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had cupping done by Abu Taybah, then he (peace be upon him) ordered that he be given two sa’ of grain, and he told his owners to take less tax from him (i.e., the levy they used to take from him). And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the medicines with which you treat yourselves, the best medicine is cupping, or he said: It is among your best medicines."
"937","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` the people of Jahiliyyah used to sell the meat of a camel until ""Habl al-Hablah."" And ""Habl al-Hablah"" is that a she-camel gives birth, then its offspring (a she-camel) becomes pregnant and gives birth; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade this."
"938","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade us from two types of sales and two types of clothing. He forbade the sale of Mulamasah and Munabadhah. The sale of Mulamasah is that a person touches another's cloth with his hand, by night or by day, and does not turn it over except for this purpose, i.e., for the sale. And Munabadhah is that a person throws his cloth towards another's cloth, and the other throws his cloth towards him, and this constitutes their sale—without seeing and without expressing mutual consent."
"939","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of pebbles and the sale involving deception."
"940","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade najsh (i.e., artificially raising the price without the intention of buying, only to increase the price)."
"941","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet those who are selling goods (ahead of them) (until they come to the market and the owners of the goods know the market price). If someone goes ahead and meets them and buys the goods, and then the owner of the goods comes to the market (and upon inquiring about the price, finds out that he has suffered a loss), then he has the option (if he wishes, he can annul the sale)."
"942","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade meeting riders (who bring goods) ahead (of their arrival in the market) and forbade a townsman from selling the goods of a villager. Tawus says: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), ""What is meant by a townsman selling for a villager?"" He said: The townsman should not act as a broker for the one coming from outside (rather, he should let him sell it himself)."
"943","‘Sayyiduna Ma'mar bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever hoards is a sinner. People said to Sa'id bin al-Musayyib: You yourself hoard, so he replied: Sayyiduna Ma'mar (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated this hadith, also used to hoard. (What is meant by this is that he did not hoard anything that people were in dire need of, rather he used to hoard olive oil, and this is permissible.)"
"944","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: When two people engage in a transaction, each of them has the option (to cancel the deal) before they separate, as long as they remain in the same place. Or until one gives the other the option (to confirm and complete the transaction). Now, if one gives the other the option (and says that he may finalize the sale), and then both agree upon it, the sale becomes binding. And if both separate after the sale and neither of them cancels it, then the sale also becomes binding."
"945","Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: The seller and the buyer both have the option (to cancel the deal) as long as they do not separate. Then if both speak the truth and clarify (any defect in the item or in the price), there will be blessing in their transaction. But if they lie and conceal (the defect), the blessing of their transaction will be erased. (Their trade will never flourish. In reality, whether it is trade, agriculture, or employment, honesty and integrity are the things due to which every work progresses by leaps and bounds, whereas the opposite only brings loss.)"
"946","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` a man mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he was deceived in transactions, so the Prophet said to him that when you make a sale, say: ""There is no deception"" (meaning, do not deceive me, or if you deceive, it will not be binding upon me). Then whenever he made a sale, he would say this (but instead of ""la khilabah,"" his tongue would utter ""la khiyabah"" because he could not pronounce the ""lam"")."
"947","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a heap of grain on the road. He put his hand inside it and found moisture on his fingers. He asked, ""O owner of the grain, what is this?"" He replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! It was wetted by rain."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then why did you not put the wet grain on top so that people could see it? Whoever deceives is not from me."
"948","Malik bin Aws bin Hadthan narrates: He says, ""I came saying, 'Who will exchange silver for gold?' Sayyiduna Talha bin Ubaidullah said—and he was sitting with Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)—'Give me your gold, then come back after a while. When our servant comes, we will give you your price.' Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, 'Never! Either give him his silver at that very moment or return his gold to him. Because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Exchanging silver for gold is usury, except when it is hand to hand; and exchanging wheat for wheat is usury, except when it is hand to hand; and exchanging barley for barley is usury, except when it is hand to hand; and exchanging dates for dates is usury, except when it is hand to hand.'"
"949","‘Sayyiduna ‘Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, and salt for salt—must be equal in amount, exactly, and hand to hand (then it is permissible). But when the types differ (for example, wheat for barley), then sell as you wish (with increase or decrease), but it must be hand to hand."
"950","Abu Al-Minhāl says: One of my partners sold silver on credit until the Hajj season and came to me and informed me. I said, ""This is not correct."" He said, ""I sold it in the market and no one forbade it."" Then I went to Sayyiduna Barā’ bin ‘Āzib (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Madinah and we used to conduct such sales. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If it is hand to hand (cash), then there is no objection, but if it is on credit, then it is usury. Go to Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), for his trading is more than mine (so he will be well aware of this issue). I went to him and asked him, and he said the same."
"951","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not sell one dinar for two dinars, nor sell one dirham for two dirhams."
"952","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was staying at Khaybar, and a necklace was brought to him which had gems and gold in it. It was from the spoils (booty) that was being sold. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that its gold be separated, so its gold was separated. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Now sell the gold for gold, by equal weight."
"953","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ata bin Abi Rabah that Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) met Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and asked him, ""What you say about the transaction of sarf (exchange of gold and silver), did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) or did you find it in the Noble Word of Allah?"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, ""By no means, I do not say anything like that. You know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) better than I do, and I do not know (this ruling) in the Book of Allah either. But Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Beware! There is usury in credit."" (However, according to some scholars, the hadith of Usama bin Zaid is abrogated in its ruling, and some have said that it will be interpreted, and that is, it applies to those properties which are not usurious, etc., or this hadith is ambiguous.)"
"954","Abu Nadrah says: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Umar and Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about (the transaction of) sarf (exchange of gold, silver, or currency), and they saw no harm in it (even if there is an increase or decrease, provided it is hand to hand). Then I was sitting with Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), so I asked him about (the transaction of) sarf. He said: ""Whatever is in excess is usury."" I denied this because of what Sayyiduna Ibn Umar and Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) had said, so he said: ""I will not narrate to you except what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" A man who had dates came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with a sa' of good quality dates, and the dates of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) were of the same kind. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Where did you get these dates from?"" He replied: ""I took two sa' of dates and bought one sa' of these dates in exchange, because its price in the market is such and its price is such."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to you, you have engaged in usury. When you want to do so, sell your dates for something else, then buy whatever dates you want with that thing."" Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""So when dates are exchanged for dates and there is usury in it, then when silver is exchanged for silver (more or less), there will definitely be usury in it (even if it is hand to hand)."" Abu Nadrah said: ""After that, I went to Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) again, and he also forbade it (perhaps he had heard the hadith of Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him). And I did not go to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), but Abu al-Sahba narrated to me that he asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about it in Makkah, and he considered it disliked."
"955","`Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed the one who consumes usury, the one who gives it, the one who writes it down, and its witnesses. And he said that they are all equal."
"956","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say—and Nu’man pointed with his fingers towards both his ears (to indicate that he heard it with his own ears)—that: “Indeed, the lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, but between the two are matters that are doubtful, which many people do not know. So whoever avoids the doubtful matters has protected his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into the doubtful matters will eventually fall into the unlawful, like a shepherd who grazes his flock near a forbidden pasture; it is likely that his flock will soon graze in it. Beware! Every king has a sanctuary, and beware! The sanctuary of Allah is His prohibited things. Know that in the body there is a piece of flesh; if it is sound, the whole body is sound, and if it is corrupt, the whole body is corrupt. Know that it is the heart.”"
"957","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man had a debt upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He demanded repayment from you (peace be upon him) harshly, so the Companions intended to punish him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one who has a right is allowed to speak (demand it)."" (This character is a proof of Prophethood.) Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Buy him a camel and give it to him."" They said: ""We only find a better camel than his."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Buy that one and give it to him, for the best among you are those who repay debts in the best manner."
"958","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Avoid excessive swearing in trade, for it may promote the sale of goods but then erases (the blessing from it)."
"959","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There are three types of people with whom Allah will neither speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them, nor will He purify them, and for them is a painful punishment. One is the person who keeps more water than he needs in the wilderness and withholds it from a traveler; the second is the person who sells something to someone after Asr prayer and swears that he bought it for such-and-such amount, and the buyer believes him, whereas he did not buy it for that amount (i.e., he swore falsely, and the mention of after Asr is because it is a blessed time when angels gather, or it is the original time for buying and selling); and the third is the person who pledges allegiance to the Imam for worldly gain. Then, if the Imam gives him some worldly goods, he fulfills his pledge, but if he does not give him, he does not fulfill it (so this person deceived the Muslims by pledging allegiance, and they relied on his promise, but he was only concerned with worldly gain and did not care about his pledge)."
"960","‘Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I participated in jihad with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He met me on the way, and my mount was a water-carrying camel that had become exhausted and could not walk at all. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “What happened to your camel?” I replied, “It is sick.” Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) moved back, scolded the camel, and prayed for it. After that, it always walked ahead of all the other camels. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “How is your camel now?” I said, “It is well by the blessing of your supplication.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Will you sell it to me?” I felt shy, and we had no other camel to bring water, but finally I said, “Yes, I will sell it.” Then I sold the camel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the condition that I would ride it until we reached Madinah. Then I said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have recently gotten married, so please allow me (to go to Madinah before the people).” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) granted me permission. I went ahead of the people and reached Madinah. There I met my uncle, who asked about the camel, so I told him the whole story. He reproached me (saying that you had only one camel and many family members, yet you sold it, and he did not know that Allah intended benefit for Sayyiduna Jabir). Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for permission, he asked, “Did you marry a virgin or a previously married woman?” I said, “A previously married woman.” He said, “Why did you not marry a virgin, so that she would play with you and you with her?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! My father passed away or was martyred, leaving behind several young sisters, so I did not like to bring another young girl like them who would neither teach them manners nor discipline them. That is why I married a previously married woman, so that she would discipline them and teach them manners.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Madinah, I brought the camel to him in the morning. He gave me its price and also returned the camel to me."
"961","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he demanded his debt from Ibn Abi Hadrad in the mosque during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so their voices became loud, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard them while he was in his house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) lifted the curtain of his room, came out to them, and called out, ""O Ka'b bin Malik!"" He replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! I am present."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gestured with his hand and said, ""Forgive half of the debt."" So Sayyiduna Ka'b said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have forgiven it."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Ibn Abi Hadrad, ""Get up and pay his debt."
"962","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever is wealthy (that is, has the ability to repay a debt) and delays in repaying the debt, it is oppression. And when any of you is referred to a wealthy person, he should follow him. (That is, if a wealthy person takes responsibility for paying the debt, it should be accepted and he should be asked for it.)"
"963","Narrated by Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet: He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A man died and entered Paradise, and he was asked: What deeds did you use to do? Then he remembered himself or was reminded, so he said: I used to sell goods to people (in the world), and I would give respite to the insolvent and overlook (their faults or losses in cash or coin and accept it). Because of this, he was forgiven. Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I also heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"964","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah that his father, Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him), demanded repayment of a debt from one of his debtors, so he hid himself. Then when he found him, the debtor said, ""I am destitute."" Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""By Allah?"" He replied, ""By Allah."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever wishes that Allah saves him from the hardships of the Day of Resurrection, let him grant respite to a destitute person or forgive (the debt) for him."
"965","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When a person becomes insolvent (that is, bankrupt), and another person finds his belongings with him, then he has a greater right to them."
"966","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah bought grain on credit for a fixed period from a Jew and pledged his iron armor with him."
"967","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Madinah, people used to do salam (forward sale) in fruits for one or two years (i.e., they used to sell on credit). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever does salam in dates should do so for a specified measure or a specified weight and for a specified period."
"968","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed the right of pre-emption (shuf‘ah) in every joint property that is undivided, whether it is land or a garden. It is not permissible for one partner to sell his share without informing the other partner. Then the other partner has the choice: if he wishes, he may take it, and if he wishes, he may leave it. Now, if it is sold without informing (the partner), then that partner has more right (he can take it himself from the outsider for the same price)."
"969","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a wooden beam (girder, rafter) in his wall (because this is against courtesy and there is no harm to oneself; rather, if the neighbor builds a roof there, it will protect the wall). Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say to the people: I see that you are turning away from this hadith; by Allah, I will surely convey it among you."
"970","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) that Arwa bint Uwais made a claim against Sa'id bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that he had taken some of her land. And she presented the case against him before Marwan bin Hakam. So Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Would I take her land? And I have heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" Marwan said, ""What have you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"" He said, ""I heard him say: Whoever unjustly seizes even a handspan of someone else's land, Allah will make him wear a collar of it down to seven earths."" Marwan said, ""Now I will not ask you for any evidence."" After this, Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Allah, if Arwa is lying, then make her blind and cause her to die in her own land."" The narrator said that Arwa did not die until she became blind, and one day she was walking in her land, fell into a pit, and died."
"971","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you disagree about the road, then keep its width seven handspans."
